## Context

Fourth round of live findings, testing v0.3.19 right after install. One
genuine correctness bug (a multi-minute display regression, not a
flicker), plus wording/content fixes from the same session.

## Findings and fixes

1. **Turning indexing off mid-first-census, then back on, regressed a
   correct "1 515 / 16 606" to a bare "0" for the length of the whole
   re-walk** — minutes, at library scale, since every activation re-hashes
   from scratch. Two contributing bugs, both fixed:
   - `getSDTCoverage()` forced "unknown" during any census phase with no
     `censusSnapshot` yet, even when the live counts were perfectly good
     to show (case: the first-ever census, interrupted before its first
     completion). Now falls back to live counts when no snapshot exists.
   - `sweep()` reset `state.counts` to `{}` at the top of every census
     with nothing capturing what was there first. Now snapshots the
     pre-reset state (when there is one) before resetting, so a restarted
     census always has something to show throughout its own re-walk,
     until it completes and overwrites the snapshot with fresh numbers.
2. **The "Indexing under way" box still blinked between documents** even
   with its reserved height (ticket 0748): the text itself flashed to "No
   indexing under way" for real, in the genuine gap `scheduler.js` awaits
   through between one document settling and the next being admitted.
   `state.pending` still names what is queued behind that gap, so the box
   now reads "Preparing the next attachment…" instead of implying nothing
   is happening.
3. **"Scanned X attachments out of Y" duplicated the census table's own
   total row** — `scanned` and the account's summed total are the same
   number by construction, since every classified attachment adds to
   both. Reworded to "{total} attachments in the library.", keeping the
   one number the table doesn't already show.
4. **The "About and limitations" disclosure opened straight into
   limitations, with no sentence saying what the plugin does.** Added an
   intro naming SDT, what a pack is, where it lives on disk
   (`.zotero-sdt-cache`, beside the attachment in its own storage folder),
   and why this assistant builds it ahead of time. The author's own call:
   "pack" may appear here, the one place the term is explained rather than
   assumed, via a scoped exception to the repo-wide vocabulary ban.

## Test

- `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs`: the `getSDTCoverage` unit case for
  "mid-census, no snapshot" updated to expect live counts, not zero; a new
  integration test drives two real `sweep()` calls (interrupt before
  completion, restart) and asserts the count survives the restart.
  Verified red against the pre-fix `scheduler.js`.
- `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs`: a new test drives the real gap between
  two admissions and asserts "Preparing the next attachment…" appears
  where "No indexing under way" is wrong. Verified red against the
  pre-fix `bootstrap.js`.
- `tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs`: the census-line wording updated; the
  About intro's presence, position, and file-path content asserted.
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`: a scoped exception added to the vocabulary
  ban for `about-intro`'s use of "pack".

## Verification

- [x] All four `.mjs` suites pass
- [x] `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`, `tests/test_sitter_host_apis.py` pass
- [x] `make check-fast` — 1313 passed, 15 skipped, no failures
- [x] Manifest/update.json bumped 0.3.19 -> 0.3.20, version guard clean
- [x] Both scheduler-level fixes verified with a positive control (red
      against the pre-fix code)

## Exit criteria

Switching indexing off and back on never shows a worse number than what
was already known. The active-file box never implies idleness while more
work is queued behind a brief admission gap. The census line and the
account table each say something the other doesn't. "About" opens with
what the plugin is, before what it cannot do.
